course: dictionary
lesson: 1941
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning is meant. Commission is one of these words. Read the whole sentence before you decide what it means.
explain: «The shop pays him commission on every phone he sells.» Pays and sells tell you this is about money. A commission here is a part of each sale that goes to the salesperson, often as a percentage: 10% commission on £500 is £50.
explain: «The government set up a commission to look into the flooding.» Here a commission is a group of people chosen to find out about something. «In the Great Commission Jesus told his followers to go to all nations» shows a commission can also be a special task given to people. Swap each meaning into the sentence to check which one fits.
fact: «Commission» can be a noun, which names a thing, or a verb, which describes an action.
fact: A commission is money paid to a salesperson as a percentage of what they sell.
fact: To commission something means to ask an artist, writer or builder to make it for you and pay them, as in «commission a painting».
fact: An official commission is a group chosen to find out about something, like a road safety commission.
fact: «Out of commission» means broken or not working.
exercise: «She earns commission on every car she sells.» What does commission mean here? | A painting made for someone | A group of people who run a town | *Money paid as a part of each sale | A rank in the army
exercise: «The museum decided to commission a new painting from a local artist.» What does commission mean here? | *To ask an artist to make a work and pay them | To break something | A ship that sails across the sea | To find out about an event
exercise: «The machine is out of commission until Monday.» What does this mean? | It is in the army | *It is broken and not working | It is very fast | It is for sale on commission
test: «The council set up a commission to investigate the bus delays.» What is the commission? | A sale of buses | *A group chosen to find out about something | A painting of a bus | A broken machine
test: A salesperson sells £500 of goods and earns 10% commission. How much commission is earned? | £5 | *£50 | £5000 | £500
exam: «In the Great Commission Jesus told his followers to go to all nations, make disciples and baptise them.» In this sentence, what is the commission? | A bill for a sale | A painting of nations | *A special task given to followers | A group of officers in the army
